        "procedure": "Under ambient conditions, Ce(NO3)3·6H2O (0.3262 g, 1 mmol) and Hacac (204 μL, 2 mmol) were dissolved in EtOH (3 mL) in a 7 mL glass vial. The solution was sonicated for 5 min, then triethylamine (557 μL, 4 mmol) was added dropwise. The solution was cooled to 15 °C. After 1 week, orange rod-like crystals of Ce-1 and an unidentified yellow–orange powder precipitated. The mother liquor was removed, the product was washed 3 × 3 mL with 1:1 EtOH/hexanes, and crystals were dried under ambient conditions for 1 h. PXRD indicated Ce-1 was a minor phase.",
